  planner_response {
    response: "Here is a recommended architecture and design blueprint for your **Private Messaging App** using 100% free-tier services and modern Android Jetpack Compose:\n\n---\n\n### **Architecture & Free-Tier Plan**\n\n1. **Backend & Real-Time Sync (Free Tier)**\n   - **Firebase Firestore Spark Plan (Free)**: Real-time listener streams (`snapshots()`) for instant messaging, delivered/read receipts, and presence indicators.\n   - **Zero-Plaintext Architecture**: All messages are encrypted client-side using **AES-256-GCM** before sending to Firestore, meaning even the database only ever stores ciphertext.\n\n2. **On-Device Storage & Security**\n   - **Room Database + Android Keystore**: Store chat history, contact keys, and encrypted local messages with offline-first support.\n   - **Privacy Shield**: Biometric/PIN app lock, `FLAG_SECURE` (blocks screenshots and screen recording), and disappearing/self-destructing message timers.\n\n3. **Design & UX Aesthetic**\n   - **Clean & Minimalist M3**: High-contrast, typography-first interface with generous negative space, OLED Dark / Warm Neutral Light modes, subtle message bubbles, and smooth gesture transitions (swipe-to-reply).\n\n---\n\n### **A Few Quick Questions to Customize Your App:**\n\n1. **User Identity & Pairing**:\n   - Would you prefer **Privacy Handle / 6-digit Invite Code / QR Code exchange** (no phone numbers or personal emails required), or standard **Google Sign-In**?\n2. **Disappearing Messages**:\n   - Should chats support customizable self-destruct timers (e.g., *View Once*, *30 seconds*, *24 hours*, or *Off*)?\n3. **Media & Voice**:\n   - Would you like text-only messaging first, or should we include encrypted image attachments and voice notes?\n4. **Theme Preference**:\n   - Do you prefer an **OLED Pure Black & Slate** aesthetic, a **Warm Minimalist Off-White/Charcoal** palette, or dynamic Material You theming?\n\nLet me know your preferences, and we will begin building right away!"
    thinking: "**Initiating Project Planning**\n\nI\'m starting to sketch out a plan for a private messaging app, aiming for a clean, minimal UI/UX design and a free-tier implementation. I\'m focusing on open-source solutions and considering the initial setup and design principles, and I\'m keen to prioritize a simple, user-friendly experience. I\'m focusing on the first steps and considering different potential components.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Core Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the essential features for the messaging app. I\'m prioritizing Room database integration for data persistence. Image generation is also on the radar for later use in assets, avatars, and icons. I\'m keeping design guidelines and user interface elements as a core focus as I build out the basic structure.\n\n\n**Analyzing Architectural Options**\n\nI\'m now diving into architectural considerations, specifically encryption methods and data storage. I\'m weighing the pros and cons of local encryption with peer-to-peer options, alongside cloud-based backends like Firebase with its free-tier benefits. Thinking about using local encrypted storage such as Room and SQLCipher, but also considering end-to-end encryption with Firebase Firestore. I\'m focusing on user privacy.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Here is a recommended architecture and design blueprint for your **Private Messaging App** using 100% free-tier services and modern Android Jetpack Compose:\n\n---\n\n### **Architecture & Free-Tier Plan**\n\n1. **Backend & Real-Time Sync (Free Tier)**\n   - **Firebase Firestore Spark Plan (Free)**: Real-time listener streams (`snapshots()`) for instant messaging, delivered/read receipts, and presence indicators.\n   - **Zero-Plaintext Architecture**: All messages are encrypted client-side using **AES-256-GCM** before sending to Firestore, meaning even the database only ever stores ciphertext.\n\n2. **On-Device Storage & Security**\n   - **Room Database + Android Keystore**: Store chat history, contact keys, and encrypted local messages with offline-first support.\n   - **Privacy Shield**: Biometric/PIN app lock, `FLAG_SECURE` (blocks screenshots and screen recording), and disappearing/self-destructing message timers.\n\n3. **Design & UX Aesthetic**\n   - **Clean & Minimalist M3**: High-contrast, typography-first interface with generous negative space, OLED Dark / Warm Neutral Light modes, subtle message bubbles, and smooth gesture transitions (swipe-to-reply).\n\n---\n\n### **A Few Quick Questions to Customize Your App:**\n\n1. **User Identity & Pairing**:\n   - Would you prefer **Privacy Handle / 6-digit Invite Code / QR Code exchange** (no phone numbers or personal emails required), or standard **Google Sign-In**?\n2. **Disappearing Messages**:\n   - Should chats support customizable self-destruct timers (e.g., *View Once*, *30 seconds*, *24 hours*, or *Off*)?\n3. **Media & Voice**:\n   - Would you like text-only messaging first, or should we include encrypted image attachments and voice notes?\n4. **Theme Preference**:\n   - Do you prefer an **OLED Pure Black & Slate** aesthetic, a **Warm Minimalist Off-White/Charcoal** palette, or dynamic Material You theming?\n\nLet me know your preferences, and we will begin building right away!"
