  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the UI components now. Specifically, the `AvatarView.kt` file. I\'m focusing on creating a monogram circle that can handle custom colors or hex codes, along with that online indicator dot. I need to make sure I get the sizing support right, with options like 40dp, 48dp, 56dp, and 72dp. Next up, I\'ll tackle the `BottomNavBar`.\n\n\n**Defining Chat UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the chat list screen\'s UI elements. I\'m focusing on the \"Messages\" header, search toggle, and vault button, along with filter chips (All, Unread, Encrypted, Groups). The chat list is getting its styling based on the provided HTML, including avatar circles, names, timestamps, and last message previews. I\'m considering unread badges, disappearing timer indicators, and pin icons for pinned chats, and I\'ve started on a FAB.\n\n\n**Constructing Conversation Screen**\n\nI\'m now deep in `ConversationScreen.kt`, working on the UI. The top bar elements are shaping up nicely: back button, peer avatar (40dp), name, status, and call/more menu. I\'ve integrated the encryption banner and the disappearing timer indicator. Now, I\'m defining the message list, with date dividers and distinct styles for peer and my messages. I\'m focusing on the bubbles with correct colors, rounded corners, and timestamp placement, incorporating reply quotes. Voice message bubbles with waveform, duration, and play/pause controls are next on my list.\n\n\n**Defining Conversation Controls**\n\nI\'m now designing the conversation\'s interactive controls. The bottom input bar is taking shape with attachment, text field, voice record, and send buttons. Next, I\'ll move on to the `StatusScreen`, defining the stories/ephemeral status elements, complete with cards and a progress indicator.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 767749569
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
