  planner_response {
    response: "I have built the **Private Messenger** application tailored to the **Clean Minimalism** design system and built for 100% free-tier, privacy-first operations:\n\n### **Design & Visual Polish**\n- **Clean Minimalism Palette**: Built with a high-contrast `#FDFBFF` canvas, deep indigo accents (`#005AC1`, `#001453`), pastel monogram avatar containers (`#DDE1FF`, `#EADDFF`, `#FDE0FF`, `#D1E4FF`), and a `#F3F3FA` surface bar.\n- **Typography & Proportions**: Applied generous negative space, refined tracking, and prominent header displays matching the Clean Minimalism design specification.\n- **Custom Adaptive Launcher Icon**: Crafted a minimalist shield lock and encrypted message bubble glyph layered over a linear indigo-to-midnight gradient.\n\n### **Core Privacy & Messaging Capabilities**\n- **Zero-Plaintext Local Encryption**: Messages and keys are secured locally using **AES-256-CBC** and **SHA-256** inside an offline-first **Room Database**.\n- **Disappearing & Self-Destruct Timers**: Supports automatic message expiration (30s, 5m, 1h, 24h) with periodic purge cycles and active countdown badges.\n- **Interactive Conversation View**:\n  - Encrypted chat bubbles with delivery/read ticks (\342\234\223, \342\234\223\342\234\223) and quote reply previews.\n  - Interactive voice note recorder & playable waveform visualizer.\n  - Attachment menu for View-Once encrypted photos, secret notes, and burn-on-read alerts.\n  - Ciphertext inspector allowing users to verify the raw AES encrypted payload stored in the database.\n- **Safety Number Verification**: 60-digit ECDH cryptographic fingerprint comparison dialog for zero-trust contact authentication.\n- **Security Vault & Stealth Shield**:\n  - **4-Digit Passcode Screen**: Keypad lock screen protecting access to the app.\n  - **Stealth Mode (`FLAG_SECURE`)**: Prevents screenshots and masks app switcher task thumbnails.\n  - **Emergency Panic Wipe**: Instant one-tap wipe of all stored chats, calls, and cryptographic keys.\n- **Ephemeral Status & P2P Call Screens**: 24-hour disappearing status updates and an encrypted voice/video call screen featuring SAS emoji verification (*Short Authentication Strings*)."
