  planner_response {
    response: "Here is how you can turn your downloaded ZIP file into an installable **APK**:\n\n---\n\n### **Method 1: Using Android Studio (Recommended & Easiest)**\n\n1. **Extract the ZIP file**:\n   - Right-click the downloaded `.zip` file on your computer and extract/unzip it into a folder.\n\n2. **Open the project in Android Studio**:\n   - Download and open [Android Studio](https://developer.android.com/studio) (free).\n   - On the welcome screen, click **Open** (or go to **File > Open**).\n   - Select the extracted project folder (the one containing `build.gradle.kts` and the `app` folder).\n   - Wait 1\342\200\2232 minutes for Gradle to automatically sync the project.\n\n3. **Build the APK**:\n   - In the top menu bar, go to **Build** \342\206\222 **Build Bundle(s) / APK(s)** \342\206\222 **Build APK(s)**.\n   - When the build finishes, a notification will pop up in the bottom-right corner saying **\"APK(s) generated successfully\"**.\n   - Click the blue **locate** link inside that notification to open the folder containing your file: `app-debug.apk`.\n\n4. **Install on your phone**:\n   - Transfer `app-debug.apk` to your Android phone via USB, Google Drive, WhatsApp, or email, tap the file on your device, and install!\n\n---\n\n### **Method 2: Using the Command Line (Terminal / Command Prompt)**\n\nIf you have Java (JDK 17 or higher) and the Android SDK installed:\n\n1. Open your **Terminal** (macOS/Linux) or **Command Prompt / PowerShell** (Windows).\n2. Navigate to your extracted project folder:\n   ```bash\n   cd path/to/extracted-folder\n   ```\n3. Run the Gradle build command:\n   - **Windows:**\n     ```cmd\n     gradlew assembleDebug\n     ```\n   - **macOS / Linux:**\n     ```bash\n     ./gradlew assembleDebug\n     ```\n4. Your finished APK will be created at:\n   ```\n   app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### **Tip for Installing on Android**\nWhen installing the APK on your phone for the first time, Android may show a standard *\"File might be harmful\"* or *\"Unknown Source\"* warning. Tap **Settings** \342\206\222 **Allow from this source** (or tap **Install Anyway**) to complete the installation."
    modified_response: "Here is how you can turn your downloaded ZIP file into an installable **APK**:\n\n---\n\n### **Method 1: Using Android Studio (Recommended & Easiest)**\n\n1. **Extract the ZIP file**:\n   - Right-click the downloaded `.zip` file on your computer and extract/unzip it into a folder.\n\n2. **Open the project in Android Studio**:\n   - Download and open [Android Studio](https://developer.android.com/studio) (free).\n   - On the welcome screen, click **Open** (or go to **File > Open**).\n   - Select the extracted project folder (the one containing `build.gradle.kts` and the `app` folder).\n   - Wait 1\342\200\2232 minutes for Gradle to automatically sync the project.\n\n3. **Build the APK**:\n   - In the top menu bar, go to **Build** \342\206\222 **Build Bundle(s) / APK(s)** \342\206\222 **Build APK(s)**.\n   - When the build finishes, a notification will pop up in the bottom-right corner saying **\"APK(s) generated successfully\"**.\n   - Click the blue **locate** link inside that notification to open the folder containing your file: `app-debug.apk`.\n\n4. **Install on your phone**:\n   - Transfer `app-debug.apk` to your Android phone via USB, Google Drive, WhatsApp, or email, tap the file on your device, and install!\n\n---\n\n### **Method 2: Using the Command Line (Terminal / Command Prompt)**\n\nIf you have Java (JDK 17 or higher) and the Android SDK installed:\n\n1. Open your **Terminal** (macOS/Linux) or **Command Prompt / PowerShell** (Windows).\n2. Navigate to your extracted project folder:\n   ```bash\n   cd path/to/extracted-folder\n   ```\n3. Run the Gradle build command:\n   - **Windows:**\n     ```cmd\n     gradlew assembleDebug\n     ```\n   - **macOS / Linux:**\n     ```bash\n     ./gradlew assembleDebug\n     ```\n4. Your finished APK will be created at:\n   ```\n   app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### **Tip for Installing on Android**\nWhen installing the APK on your phone for the first time, Android may show a standard *\"File might be harmful\"* or *\"Unknown Source\"* warning. Tap **Settings** \342\206\222 **Allow from this source** (or tap **Install Anyway**) to complete the installation."
