    response: "Here are the exact step-by-step commands to push your project from that path to **GitHub**:\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Open Terminal & Navigate to the Folder**\n\nOpen **Command Prompt**, **PowerShell**, or **Git Bash** on your computer, then copy and paste this command:\n\n```cmd\ncd C:\\Users\\abhis\\Downloads\\private-messenger\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Initialize Git and Prepare Files**\n\nRun these commands one by one:\n\n```cmd\ngit init\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit: Clean Minimalism Private Messenger\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit branch -M main\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Create a New GitHub Repository**\n\n1. Go to [github.com/new](https://github.com/new) in your web browser.\n2. Enter a repository name (for example: `private-messenger`).\n3. Leave it as **Public** or **Private**.\n4. **Important**: Do **NOT** check \"Add a README file\", \".gitignore\", or \"license\" (leave them unchecked).\n5. Click **Create repository**.\n6. Copy the repository URL (e.g. `https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/private-messenger.git`).\n\n---\n\n### **Step 4: Link and Push to GitHub**\n\nReplace `YOUR_USERNAME` and `YOUR_REPOSITORY` with your actual GitHub link and run:\n\n```cmd\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/private-messenger.git\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push -u origin main\n```\n\n*(If prompted, log in with your GitHub credentials or a Personal Access Token).*\n\n---\n\n### **Summary of all commands in one block:**\n\n```cmd\ncd C:\\Users\\abhis\\Downloads\\private-messenger\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit\"\ngit branch -M main\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/private-messenger.git\ngit push -u origin main\n```"
